2. ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION OF UNAUTHORIZED ACTS
--------------------------------------------
Except strictly to the extent required by mandatory, non-waivable statutory
provisions of applicable law (such as non-derogable fair dealing provisions
under Section 52 of the Indian Copyright Act, 1957, or mandatory reverse
engineering provisions under Article 5(3) and Article 6 of EU Directive 2009/24/EC
that cannot be contractually altered), NO PERMISSION, LICENSE, IMMUNITY, OR
AUTHORIZATION (WHETHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED, BY ESTOPPEL, OR OTHERWISE) IS GRANTED.

Under Research expressly prohibits any individual, company, organization,
governmental entity, or third party from performing any of the following acts
without prior, express, written authorization executed by Under Research:

  (a) COPYING & REPRODUCTION: You shall not copy, duplicate, reproduce, clone,
      fork, mirror, snapshot, store, archive, scrape, or cache the Software, or
      any portion, file, class, function, method, AST, or line of code thereof,
      in any physical, digital, cloud, or virtual medium.

  (b) MODIFICATION & DERIVATIVE WORKS: You shall not modify, adapt, alter, edit,
      patch, translate, refactor, enhance, combine, or prepare derivative works
      based upon the Software or any portion thereof.

  (c) DISTRIBUTION & DISSEMINATION: You shall not distribute, publish, broadcast,
      circulate, share, transmit, transfer, convey, publicly display, publicly
      perform, or communicate the Software to the public through any medium,
      repository, package index, package manager, or network channel.

  (d) COMMERCIAL EXPLOITATION & SUBLICENSING: You shall not sell, resell, lease,
      rent, loan, sublicense, distribute, package, or commercially exploit the
      Software, or provide access to its functionality as a service (SaaS),
      managed service, cloud offering, or hosted solution.

  (e) REBRANDING & REPACKAGING: You shall not repackage, rebrand, rename, or
      redistribute the Software, or any derivative or subset thereof, under a
      different name, moniker, trade name, organization, or corporate entity.

  (f) REVERSE ENGINEERING: You shall not decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer,
      or attempt to reconstruct or discover the source code, internal logic, or
      underlying algorithms of any binary, byte-compiled, or obfuscated component,
      except strictly where such prohibition is expressly invalid under
      non-waivable statutory law.

  (g) ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE & MACHINE LEARNING INGESTION: You shall not use,
      ingest, scrape, tokenize, or process the Software, its code, structure, or
      documentation as training data, fine-tuning data, validation data, or
