3. MULTI-JURISDICTIONAL LEGAL ENFORCEMENT & RIGHT TO SUE
--------------------------------------------------------
Under Research actively audits and vigorously protects its intellectual property
globally.

Any unauthorized copying, cloning, forking, reproduction, extraction,
distribution, modification, reverse engineering, commercial use, or infringement
of this Software constitutes an intentional, willful violation of applicable
intellectual property and computer protection laws across jurisdictions, including:

  (i)   INTERNATIONAL TREATIES & CONVENTIONS:
        - The Berne Convention for the Protection of Literary and Artistic Works;
        - The WIPO Copyright Treaty (WCT);
        - The Universal Copyright Convention (UCC); and
        - The Agreement on Trade-Related Aspects of Intellectual Property Rights
          (TRIPS Agreement).

  (ii)  INDIA:
        - Section 51 and Section 55 of the Indian Copyright Act, 1957 (Infringement
          and Civil Remedies);
        - Sections 73 and 74 of the Indian Contract Act, 1872 (Breach of Contract);
        - Specific Relief Act, 1963 (Injunctions and Specific Enforcement); and
        - Section 43 and Section 66 of the Information Technology Act, 2000
          (Unauthorized copying, extraction, and downloading of computer data/code).

  (iii) UNITED STATES:
        - Title 17 of the United States Code (U.S. Copyright Act, 17 U.S.C. § 101
          et seq., including § 501 Infringement);
        - The Digital Millennium Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 1201 Anti-Circumvention
          and § 1202 Integrity of Copyright Management Information);
        - The Defend Trade Secrets Act of 2016 (DTSA, 18 U.S.C. § 1836 et seq.)
          and applicable state Uniform Trade Secrets Acts (UTSA); and
        - The Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA, 18 U.S.C. § 1030).

  (iv)  UNITED KINGDOM & COMMONWEALTH:
        - The Copyright, Designs and Patents Act 1988 (CDPA 1988);
        - The Computer Misuse Act 1990;
        - The Australian Copyright Act 1968; and
        - The Singapore Copyright Act 2021.

  (v)   EUROPEAN UNION:
        - Directive 2009/24/EC on the legal protection of computer programs;
        - Directive 2001/29/EC (InfoSoc Directive);
        - Directive (EU) 2016/943 on the protection of undisclosed know-how and
          business information (Trade Secrets Directive); and
        - Directive (EU) 2019/790 on copyright in the Digital Single Market.

IN THE EVENT OF ANY INFRINGEMENT OR BREACH, UNDER RESEARCH RESERVES ALL RIGHTS
TO INITIATE IMMEDIATE CIVIL LITIGATION AND PURSUE ALL REMEDIES AVAILABLE AT LAW
AND IN EQUITY IN ANY COURT OF COMPETENT JURISDICTION, INCLUDING:

  (a) IMMEDIATE INJUNCTIVE RELIEF: The user acknowledges that unauthorized
      copying, disclosure, or distribution causes immediate, irreversible, and
      irreparable harm to Under Research for which monetary damages alone are
      inadequate. Under Research shall be entitled to seek and obtain immediate
      ex-parte temporary restraining orders (TROs), preliminary injunctions,
      interlocutory injunctions, permanent injunctions, search and seizure orders
      (including Anton Piller orders), asset-freezing orders (Mareva injunctions),
      and John Doe / Ashok Kumar orders from any competent court worldwide
      without the necessity of proving actual monetary damages or posting a bond.

  (b) ACTUAL DAMAGES, STATUTORY DAMAGES & DISGORGEMENT OF PROFITS: Under
      Research shall be entitled to seek and recover all actual economic damages
      suffered, statutory damages where provided by applicable law (such as under
      17 U.S.C. § 504), full restitution, and an accounting and disgorgement of
      all revenues, gross profits, and commercial advantages derived by the
      infringing party from the unauthorized handling of the Software.

  (c) LEGAL FEES & INVESTIGATION COSTS: To the fullest extent permitted under
      applicable law, the infringing party shall be strictly liable to reimburse
      Under Research for all attorney's fees, advocate fees, court costs, expert
      witness fees, and forensic/investigative expenses incurred in identifying,
      halting, and litigating the infringement.

  (d) IMPOUNDMENT, SEIZURE & DESTRUCTION: Under Research shall be entitled to an
      order mandating the immediate impoundment, delivery up, deletion, and
      irreversible destruction of all infringing copies, forks, mirrors, and
      derivative works, together with all storage media holding the same.


